[s0l0!-header][h1]The switch Expression[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

The [b]switch expression[/b] allows multiple comma-separated values per case and returns a value for the whole switch-case block.

[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="java" codeId="3368"]String dayType  = switch(day) {
            case 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 -> "Working day";
            case 6, 7 -> "Weekend";
            default -> "Invalid day";
            };
[/code]
The switch expression makes the switch-case block much shorter and doesn't use a break statement.

[note]Notice the [b]-> shorthand[/b] after the cases.[/note]

